 "notModeled": [
  "analog input (fully differential, +/-Vref), internal 4.096-V reference, COMMOUT (REFIN/2) and the internal 3-V regulator (CAP1/CAP2): the result is always the 0 V code 0000h (twos complement)",
  "pin 43: the pin drawing (p.7) labels it +VA but the terminal table lists +VA as pins 4 and 46 only; modeled as +VA",
  "RESET/PD1: a low pulse shorter than 0.5 us resets the ADC (conversion aborted); held low longer than 1.5 us it also powers the ADC down (5 us resume; data bus three-stated td9 1.5 us after PD1 low); the model treats it as reset only",
  "PD2 (power-down of the REFOUT/COMMOUT buffers; PD1 = 1, PD2 = 0 reserved) is not read",
  "CONVST high at the end of conversion starts sampling at once, else at CONVST rising; CONVST high time >= 100 ns, period >= 250 ns; quiet zones (30 ns before, 10 ns after CONVST falling)",
  "data appears on the bus after a conversion when CS = RD = 0 (td2 225 ns after CONVST low); reading during a conversion returns the previous result on the part (the model always returns the 0 V code)",
  "byte mode: with BYTE high DB15-DB8 carry D7-D0 and DB7-DB0 are all ones (Table 2); BYTE-to-data td5 20 ns"
 ],
